All three functions are implemented and `python3 test_impl.py` now prints `ALL PASS` (stress loop took 2.8s). I ran the suite after each function; the first two runs failed only on the next unimplemented function, as expected.

- **`encode`** (`rle.py`): groups consecutive characters and emits each character followed by its run length.
- **`decode`** (`rle.py`): reads each character-plus-digits pair and expands it.
- **`merge`** (`intervals.py`): sorts by start and folds each interval into the previous one when it overlaps or touches.

The format is ambiguous if the input string itself contains digits (e.g. `encode("111")` gives `"13"`, which also reads as one `1` repeated 3 times… but `"a1"` followed by a literal `2` would not round-trip). The docstrings and tests don't cover that case, so I left it alone.

`test_impl.py` is untouched; the changes are uncommitted, and running the tests left an untracked `__pycache__/` directory.
